"""Well-known shops, brands and services in Germany, the rest of Europe and the US, by category.

Format, one or more entries per line, separated by commas:
    Name                       matches the name as whole words, anywhere in the booking text
    Name = OTHER SPELLING / X  also matches the other spellings; Name is what lists show
    ^Name                      only when the payee starts with it (for names that are also ordinary
                               words, such as Target, Coop, Boots)
Umlauts and accents may be written as they are: "Müller" also finds MUELLER and MULLER, and names of
two or three words also match written together ("Burger King" finds BURGERKING).

Single words shorter than four letters ("KFC", "OMV") count only at the start of the payee by themselves. A word that is
also an everyday word or a common first or family name in any European language must start with "^"
or be written with a second word ("Albert Heijn", not "Albert"). tests/test_vendors.py checks both.
Bump seed.KNOWLEDGE after changing this list so existing installs sort their bookings again.
"""

